<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait import payments edge up in Feb month/month.</title>
<headline>Kuwait import payments edge up in Feb month/month.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Payments made by banks in Kuwait to finance imports rose slightly to 113.2 million dinars in February from 111.8 million in January, a Central Bank monthly bulletin said.</p>
<p>The payments were 109.9 million dinars in February 1996.</p>
<p>			   Figures in millions of dinars</p>
<p>					Feb	   Jan	 Feb '96</p>
<p>Documentary LCs		   79.1	  81.0	 84.7</p>
<p>Bills for collection	    15.2	  16.1	 14.6</p>
<p>Other payment orders	    18.9	  14.7	 10.6</p>
<p>The relative importance of the U.S. dollar in the financing rose to 60.7 percent in February from 60.5 in January. That of the Japanese yen rose to nine percent from 7.6 percent.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in figures are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.302 dinar)</p>
</text>
